# Copy this file to .env and adjust. .env is gitignored and never committed.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Everything here has a working default, so the app runs unconfigured for local
# development. Only SESSION_SECRET and CSRF_SECRET genuinely must be changed
# before you put the site on the internet.

# --- Site identity -----------------------------------------------------------
# The repo ships neutral defaults; set these to make the site your own.
# Nothing here is baked into the source, so your branding stays out of git.

# Shown in the header, the viewer gate, and the browser tab.
VITE_SITE_NAME=Travel Globe
VITE_SITE_TAGLINE=Enter the password to continue
VITE_SITE_DESCRIPTION=A private travel blog with an interactive 3D globe

# Your logo: drop a logo.png into frontend/public/branding/ (gitignored). The
# frontend build copies it over the placeholder. No variable needed.

# Domain nginx serves and looks for TLS certificates under, as
# /etc/letsencrypt/live/$SITE_DOMAIN/. Used by docker-compose.yml only;
# docker-compose.local.yml serves plain HTTP and ignores it.
SITE_DOMAIN=localhost

# Public URL of the site. Sent as the User-Agent and Referer on Nominatim
# geocoding requests, whose usage policy requires identifying the application.
SITE_URL=http://localhost:5173
SITE_NAME=Travel Globe

# --- Server ------------------------------------------------------------------
PORT=3001
NODE_ENV=development

# Frontend URL (for CORS)
FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:5173

# Upload size limit is not configurable here: it is set in two places that must
# agree: multer in backend/src/routes/upload.ts and client_max_body_size in
# frontend/nginx-app.conf. Both are 200MB.

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# CHANGE BOTH before deploying. Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
SESSION_SECRET=change-this-to-a-random-string-in-production
CSRF_SECRET=csrf-secret-change-this-in-production

# --- Production --------------------------------------------------------------
# NODE_ENV=production
# SITE_DOMAIN=example.com
# SITE_URL=https://example.com
# FRONTEND_URL=https://example.com
